This directory contains an Android Studio (2.1.1) project that builds
libwebsockets (+ openssl + zlib) and an Android application that is able
to connect to the 'dumb-increment-protocol' of the libwebsockets test server.

Building the native libraries requires the Android NDK which can be
installed using the SDK manager.

To install the Android NDK follow these steps:

 1. Download android ndk-r12b https://github.com/android/ndk/wiki/Unsupported-Downloads

 2. Download android sdk wget https://dl.google.com/android/repository/tools_r25.2.3-linux.zip

 3. Download and install java:
    sudo apt update
    sudo apt install default-jre

    Check java is installed:
    java -version

 4. Install make and cmake:
    sudo apt install make
    sudo apt install cmake

 5. Install python:
    sudo apt install python

 6. Go to end2end-smkex/android-client

 7. Export your ndk and sdk path to PATH: export ANDROID_NDK_ROOT=...
    export ANDROID_SDK_ROOT=...

 8. Create a file named "local.properties: inside android-client dir. Edit the file using the following convention:
    # SDK Path
    sdk.dir=/home/marius/Android/Sdk

    # NDK Path
    ndk.dir=/home/marius/work/kit/android-ndk-r12b/

    # SMKEX Configuration
    smkex.opensips.server=195.95.167.231
    smkex.opensips.port=8890
    smkex.server1=195.95.167.231
    smkex.server1.port=8083
    smkex.server2=141.85.232.41
    smkex.server2.port=8443
    smkex.credentials.username=root
    smkex.credentials.password=smkex

 9. Run build_apk.sh -c

 10. The binary will be available at: end2end-smkex/android-client/app/build/outputs/apk/debug

 11. Install adb: sudo apt-get install android-tools-adb

    Important: Everytime you compile the binary, you need to reload the path to the binary for example:
    - if your current path is: end2end-smkex/android-client/app/build/outputs/apk/debug
    - cd back and then again to debug. For example:
    cd ..
    cd debug
    This is necessary because the program will write a new debug dir.


The app/src/main/jni/NativeLibs.mk is fully integraded with Gradle but will
only work on Linux and requires the following applications to be available
in addition to the NDK:

   awk cmake egrep git tar wget makedepend

(makedepend can be installed from (Debian) xutils-dev)

To build the project:

- Open an 'existing project' with Android Studio and select this directory.
  (answer yes/ok to the question to integrate with Gradle).

- Open the file app/src/main/jni/Application.mk and make sure NDK_ROOT
  is set correctly and that APP_PLATFORM is set to the appropriate API level.

- Build the project with CTRL+F9
  (open the gradle console to follow the build progress).

- Install APK to device and run.

- Connect to libwebsockets test server.